        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"hi\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44b\" role=\"img\" title=\"hi\">:hi:</span> Related to this, I've been working on defining Control functions which in a sense are an abstraction of the essential properties of p-variation.</p>\n<p>I will open a PR soon: but in short I've</p>\n<ul>\n<li>defined structures <code>Control</code> and <code>ControlOn</code></li>\n<li>shown several basic properties (mostly from [1])</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I will show that if a function satisfies that <code>fun s t ↦ edist (f s) (f t) ≤ ω s t</code> for some <code>ω : ControlOn α s</code> then <code>BoundedVariationOn f s</code> and <code>eVariationOn f s ≤ ω</code></p>\n<p>A similar statement is true for p-variation as well.</p>\n<p>References<br>\n[1] : <a href=\"https://page.math.tu-berlin.de/~friz/master4_May6th.pdf\">https://page.math.tu-berlin.de/~friz/master4_May6th.pdf</a> Sections 1 and 5</p>",
        "id": 584979262,
        "sender_full_name": "Nikolas Tapia",
        "timestamp": 1775939246
    },
